# The build context is the monorepo root (see apps/vue-json-forms-builder/Dockerfile).
# Keep it small: `turbo prune` only needs manifests + sources. Note: nested
# .dockerignore files are ignored by Docker, only this root one applies.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
**/.turbo
**/.nuxt
**/.output
**/dist
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
tmp
/docs
extern
apps/demo
apps/vue-json-forms-builder/data
apps/vue-json-forms-builder/keycloak
apps/vue-json-forms-builder/docker
# Local env/secret files - change constantly, never needed in the image
# (the compose env_file values are injected at runtime, not baked in)
.env*
apps/vue-json-forms-builder/.env.docker.*
# Editor configs
**/.vscode
# Regenerated code (ajv-validator writes src/generated/*, turbo regenerates it)
**/src/generated
# Docs & tests are not needed to build or run the app, but they change on
# nearly every commit - excluding them keeps the Docker cache warm.
# (If you later add `check-types` to the Docker build, un-ignore tests.)
apps/vue-json-forms-builder/docs
apps/vue-json-forms-builder/tests
